IGC v2.28.4: MergeAllocas compile time. Still present on intel-graphics-compiler master (2026-11).

For each allocation, AllocationLivenessAnalyzer::LivenessData walks the block where its lifetime
starts up to the allocation's first user, and built a LivenessInstruction for every instruction on the
way, whose constructor finds the instruction's index by scanning the block from its start
(getInstructionIndex): quadratic in the distance walked. The index is now counted along the walk; the
lifetime start it records, and so the merging, are the same.

--- a/IGC/AdaptorCommon/LivenessUtils/AllocationLivenessAnalyzer.cpp
+++ b/IGC/AdaptorCommon/LivenessUtils/AllocationLivenessAnalyzer.cpp
@@ -285,8 +285,13 @@
   auto *lifetimeStartBB = *bbOutOnly.begin();
 
   // fill out the lifetime start/ends instruction
+  // (the index is counted along the walk; LivenessInstruction(&I) finds it by scanning the
+  // block from its start, which made this loop quadratic in the block's length)
+  size_t lifetimeStartIndex = 0;
   for (auto &I : *lifetimeStartBB) {
-    lifetimeStart = LivenessInstruction(&I, bbToIndexMap);
+    lifetimeStart.inst = &I;
+    lifetimeStart.instIndexInBB = lifetimeStartIndex++;
+    lifetimeStart.parentBBIndex = bbToIndexMap.lookup(lifetimeStartBB);
     if (usersOfAllocation.contains(&I))
       break;
   }
